  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>⊝</mo></mrow></msup></math> can act as a nucleophile also but always acts as a base. <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>⊝</mo></mrow></msup></math> is ideal to interact with the H atom's of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbital <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> (X can be any atom) but much small to interact easily with carbon's more diffuse 2p orbital <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>.<br />",
